Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II

Hilchos Hefker v&rsquo;Nichsay HaGer

Halacha 4

Whoever comes first to the property of the ger acquires it, and the matter of hefker [ownerless property] &mdash; whoever comes first to it acquires it; however, one must specifically acquire it through some act of acquisition, according to the kinyan [mode of acquisition] through which the item is acquired &mdash; for example, meshichah [pulling] and hagbahah [lifting] for movable property, and chazakah [an act of possession] for land. But without this, one does not acquire it, as is explained in the Shulchan Aruch in siman 273, se&rsquo;if 11, and this is its language: &ldquo;An ownerless item that someone came and watched over it, and was looking at it so that no person should take it &mdash; he has not acquired it until he lifts it, if it is movable, or performs chazakah on land in the manner that purchasers acquire.&rdquo; End quote.

&sect;1

